<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shkumbin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Shkumbin is a river in central Albania, about 180 kilometres long, flowing west past <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbasan">Elbasan</a> to the Adriatic. In Roman times the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/via-egnatia">Via Egnatia</a> followed its valley, making it the main route from the Adriatic coast into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>. The river is traditionally taken as the boundary between the two main Albanian dialects, Gheg in the north and Tosk in the south.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shkumbin.jpg" alt="Shkumbin" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Albinfo at de.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shkumbin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
